* PedalKernel BJT Transistor Models — SPICE .MODEL format
*
* Standard SPICE BJT parameters (Gummel-Poon / Ebers-Moll compatible):
*   IS  — Saturation current (A)
*   BF  — Forward current gain (hFE)
*   BR  — Reverse current gain
*   NF  — Forward ideality factor
*   NR  — Reverse ideality factor
*   VT  — Thermal voltage (V), default 25.85mV @ 25°C
*   VAF — Forward Early voltage (V)
*   VAR — Reverse Early voltage (V)
*   IKF — Forward knee current (A)
*   IKR — Reverse knee current (A)
*   ISE — B-E leakage saturation current (A)
*   ISC — B-C leakage saturation current (A)
*   NE  — B-E leakage ideality factor
*   NC  — B-C leakage ideality factor
*   RB  — Base resistance (Ω)
*   RE  — Emitter resistance (Ω)
*   RC  — Collector resistance (Ω)
*   CJE — Zero-bias B-E junction capacitance (F)
*   VJE — B-E built-in potential (V)
*   MJE — B-E grading coefficient
*   CJC — Zero-bias B-C junction capacitance (F)
*   VJC — B-C built-in potential (V)
*   MJC — B-C grading coefficient
*   TF  — Forward transit time (s)
*   TR  — Reverse transit time (s)
*
* Engineering suffixes: f=1e-15, p=1e-12, n=1e-9, u=1e-6, m=1e-3, k=1e3, MEG=1e6
*
* Sources: ON Semi, Fairchild, Philips, Mullard datasheets & SPICE libraries

* ── NPN Silicon ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

