* ── Germanium PNP ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

* Active: DAFx-2017 vintage-extracted AC128 (Holmes/Holters/van Walstijn). Parameters
* extracted from real vintage AC128 germanium parts and audio-validated against measured
* devices. Source: "Improving Elementary Wave Digital Models of the Fuzz Face / OC44 family",
* DAFx-2017, https://www.dafx17.eca.ed.ac.uk/papers/DAFx17_paper_28.pdf and the companion
* model repo https://github.com/grwhitehead/germaniumbjts . With this model the Fuzz Face
* biases Q2 in the active region and holds rock-solid (verified in ngspice: Q2 ~7.5V Vce,
* ~128uA Ic, <1mV drift over 400ms), so both the published deck and the canonical FF topology
* are alive. NOTE: this model biases Q2 HOT (toward the cold rail, not the textbook -4.5V
* center) — real Ge Fuzz Faces use a bias trim; centering is a separate follow-up, NOT a
* reason to retune these vintage-extracted params. ngspice-native cap params (CJE/CJC).
.MODEL AC128 PNP(IS=20.66u BF=229.6 BR=14.66 NF=1.133 NR=1.140 VAF=19.68 VAR=88.28 IKF=463m IKR=241.5m ISE=2.190u ISC=7.546u NE=1.796 NC=1.364 RB=1.885 RE=306.4m RC=1.727u CJE=100p VJE=0.3 MJE=0.5 CJC=100p VJC=0.3 MJC=0.5 TF=1n TR=100n)
* Retired: tuned-to-SPICE-reference model — IS=2.5u BF=120 NF=1.1. Found to bias the Fuzz
* Face DEAD: Q2 sits in cutoff / floating (collector pinned, transistor not conducting), so
* the WDF FF settled to a near-zero dead operating point. Superseded by the DAFx-2017 model.
*.MODEL AC128 PNP(IS=2.5u BF=120 BR=3.0 NF=1.1 NR=1.0 VAF=50 VAR=20 IKF=100m IKR=10m ISE=5n ISC=1n NE=1.8 NC=1.5 RB=30 RE=0.5 RC=1.5 CJE=40p VJE=0.3 MJE=0.4 CJC=25p VJC=0.4 MJC=0.35 TF=500p TR=50n)
.MODEL OC44 PNP(IS=1.423u BF=307 BR=20.27 NF=1.022 NR=1.025 VAF=8.167 VAR=14.84 IKF=43.82m IKR=611.7m ISE=30.54n ISC=213.5n NE=1.316 NC=1.258 RB=32.83 RE=968.7m RC=989.9u CJE=410p VJE=0.3 MJE=0.5 CJC=10p VJC=0.3 MJC=0.5 TF=1.5n TR=150n)
.MODEL NKT275 PNP(IS=1.5u BF=85 BR=8.0 NF=1.05 NR=1.05 VAF=40 VAR=20 IKF=50m IKR=20m ISE=10n ISC=1n NE=1.5 NC=1.3 RB=20 RE=0.5 RC=0.5 CJE=80p VJE=0.3 MJE=0.5 CJC=30p VJC=0.3 MJC=0.5 TF=1.2n TR=120n)

